        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "987233bd-4692-5f1d-8c72-05807fc7590e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hong Kong, Lantau Island, Ngong Ping, Diamond Hill, Nei Lak Shan\n- Organizations: Po Lin Monastery, Chi Lin Nunnery\n- Products: Tian Tan Buddha\n- Topics: Buddhism in Hong Kong, tourism\n\nFacts:\n- Chi Lin Nunnery is a prominent Buddhist temple in Hong Kong located in Diamond Hill and built in the Tang Dynasty architectural style.\n- Tian Tan Buddha is a large bronze statue of Buddha Shakyamuni in Ngong Ping on Lantau Island in Hong Kong.\n- Tian Tan Buddha was completed in 1993.\n- Po Lin Monastery is a prominent Buddhist temple on Lantau Island in Hong Kong.\n- Po Lin Monastery is famous for the nearby outdoor bronze statue Tian Tan Buddha.\n- Tian Tan Buddha and Po Lin Monastery are both significant tourist attractions.\n- Nei Lak Shan is 751 m high on Lantau Island and lies immediately north of Ngong Ping, where Po Lin Monastery is located.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
